0A\0A/** Set the password for a password-authenticated key exchange from key ID.\0A *\0A * Call this function when the password, or a value derived from the password,\0A * is already present in the key store.\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation     The operation object to set the password for. It\0A *                              must have been set up by psa_pake_setup() and\0A *                              not yet in use (neither psa_pake_output() nor\0A *                              psa_pake_input() has been called yet). It must\0A *                              be on operation for which the password hasn't\0A *                              been set yet (psa_pake_set_password_key()\0A *                              hasn't been called yet).\0A * \5Cparam password              Identifier of the key holding the password or a\0A *                              value derived from the password (eg. by a\0A *                              memory-hard function).  It must remain valid\0A *                              until the operation terminates. It must be of\0A *                              type #PSA_KEY_TYPE_PASSWORD or\0A *                              #PSA_KEY_TYPE_PASSWORD_HASH. It has to allow\0A *                              the usage #PSA_KEY_USAGE_DERIVE.\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS\0A *         Success.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE\0A *         \5Cp password is not a valid key identifier.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_NOT_PERMITTED\0A *         The key does not have the #PSA_KEY_USAGE_DERIVE flag, or it does not\0A *         permit the \5Cp operation's algorithm.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\0A *         The key type for \5Cp password is not #PSA_KEY_TYPE_PASSWORD or\0A *         #PSA_KEY_TYPE_PASSWORD_HASH, or \5Cp password is not compatible with\0A *         the \5Cp operation's cipher suite.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED\0A *         The key type or key size of \5Cp password is not supported with the\0A *         \5Cp operation's cipher suite.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_STORAGE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_DATA_CORRUPT \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_DATA_INVALID \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         The operation state is not valid (it must have been set up.), or\0A *         the library has not been previously initialized by psa_crypto_init().\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_pake_set_password_key(psa_pake_operation_t *operation,\0A                                       mbedtls_svc_key_id_t password);\0A\0A/** Set the user ID for a password-authenticated key exchange.\0A *\0A * Call this function to set the user ID. For PAKE algorithms that associate a\0A * user identifier with each side of the session you need to call\0A * psa_pake_set_peer() as well. For PAKE algorithms that associate a single\0A * user identifier with the session, call psa_pake_set_user() only.\0A *\0A * Refer to the documentation of individual PAKE algorithm types (`PSA_ALG_XXX`\0A * values of type ::psa_algorithm_t such that #PSA_ALG_IS_PAKE(\5Cc alg) is true)\0A * for more information.\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation     The operation object to set the user ID for. It\0A *                              must have been set up by psa_pake_setup() and\0A *                              not yet in use (neither psa_pake_output() nor\0A *                              psa_pake_input() has been called yet). It must\0A *                              be on operation for which the user ID hasn't\0A *                              been set (psa_pake_set_user() hasn't been\0A *                              called yet).\0A * \5Cparam[in] user_id           The user ID to authenticate with.\0A * \5Cparam user_id