                             been set (psa_pake_set_peer() hasn't been\0A *                              called yet).\0A * \5Cparam[in] peer_id           The peer's ID to authenticate.\0A * \5Cparam peer_id_len           Size of the \5Cp peer_id buffer in bytes.\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS\0A *         Success.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\0A *         \5Cp peer_id is not valid for the \5Cp operation's algorithm and cipher\0A *         suite.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED\0A *         The algorithm doesn't associate a second identity with the session.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_MEMORY \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         Calling psa_pake_set_peer() is invalid with the \5Cp operation's\0A *         algorithm, the operation state is not valid, or the library has not\0A *         been previously initialized by psa_crypto_init().\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_pake_set_peer(psa_pake_operation_t *operation,\0A                               const uint8_t *peer_id,\0A                               size_t peer_id_len);\0A\0A/** Set the application role for a password-authenticated key exchange.\0A *\0A * Not all PAKE algorithms need to differentiate the communicating entities.\0A * It is optional to call this function for PAKEs that don't require a role\0A * to be specified. For such PAKEs the application role parameter is ignored,\0A * or #PSA_PAKE_ROLE_NONE can be passed as \5Cc role.\0A *\0A * Refer to the documentation of individual PAKE algorithm types (`PSA_ALG_XXX`\0A * values of type ::psa_algorithm_t such that #PSA_ALG_IS_PAKE(\5Cc alg) is true)\0A * for more information.\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation     The operation object to specify the\0A *                              application's role for. It must have been set up\0A *                              by psa_pake_setup() and not yet in use (neither\0A *                              psa_pake_output() nor psa_pake_input() has been\0A *                              called yet). It must be on operation for which\0A *                              the application's role hasn't been specified\0A *                              (psa_pake_set_role() hasn't been called yet).\0A * \5Cparam role                  A value of type ::psa_pake_role_t indicating the\0A *                              application's role in the PAKE the algorithm\0A *                              that is being set up. For more information see\0A *                              the documentation of \5Cc PSA_PAKE_ROLE_XXX\0A *                              constants.\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS\0A *         Success.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\0A *         The \5Cp role is not a valid PAKE role in the \5Cp operation’s algorithm.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED\0A *         The \5Cp role for this algorithm is not supported or is not valid.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         The operation state is not valid, or\0A *         the library has not been previously initialized by psa_crypto_init().\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_pake_set_role(psa_pake_operation_t *operation,\0A                               psa_pake_role_t role);\0A\0A/** Get output for a step of a password-authenticated key exchange.\0A *\0A * Depending on the algorithm being executed, you might need to call this\0A * function several times or you might not need to call this at all.\0A *\0A * The exact sequence of calls to perform a password-authenticated key\0A * exchange depends on the algorithm in use.  Refer to the documentation of\0A * individual PAKE algorithm types (`PSA_ALG_XXX` values of type\0A * ::psa_algorithm_t such that #PSA_ALG_IS_PAKE(\5Cc alg) is true) for more\0A * information.\0A *\0A * If this function returns an error status, the operation enters an error\0A * state and must be aborted by calling psa_pake_abort().\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation    Active PAKE operation.\0A * \5Cparam step                 The step of the algorithm for which the output is\0A *                             requested.\0A * \5Cparam[out] output          Buffer where the output is to be written in the\0A *                             format appropriate for this \5Cp step. Refer to\0A *                             the documentation of the individual\0A *                             \5Cc PSA_PAKE_STEP_XXX constants for more\0A *                             information.\0A * \5Cparam output_size          Size of the \5Cp output buffer in bytes. This must\0A *                             be at least #PSA_PAKE_OUTPUT_SIZE(\5Cc alg, \5Cc\0A *                             primitive, \5Cp output_step) where \5Cc alg and\0A *                             \5Cp primitive are the PAKE algorithm and primitive\0A *                             in the operation's cipher suite, and \5Cp step is\0A *                             the output step.\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[out] output_length   On success, the number of bytes of the returned\0A *                             output.\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS\0A *         Success.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL\0A *         The size of the \5Cp output buffer is too small.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\0A *         \5Cp step is not compatible with the operation's algorithm.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED\0A *         \5Cp step is not supported with the operation's algorithm.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_ENTROPY \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_MEMORY \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_STORAGE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_DATA_CORRUPT \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_DATA_INVALID \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         The operation state is not valid (it must be active, and fully set\0A *         up, and this call must conform to the algorithm's requirements\0A *         for ordering of input and output steps), or\0A *         the library has not been previously initialized by psa_crypto_init().\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_pake_output(psa_pake_operation_t *operation,\0A                             psa_pake_step_t step,\0A                             uint8_t *output,\0A                             size_t output_size,\0A                             size_t *output_length);\0A\0A/** Provide input for a step of a password-authenticated key exchange.\0A *\0A * Depending on the algorithm being executed, you might need to call this\0A * function several times or you might not need to call this at all.\0A *\0A * The exact sequence of calls to perform a password-authenticated key\0A * exchange depends on the algorithm in use.  Refer to the documentation of\0A * individual PAKE algorithm types (`PSA_ALG_XXX` values of type\0A * ::psa_algorithm_t such that #PSA_ALG_IS_PAKE(\5Cc alg) is true) for more\0A * information.\0A *\0A * If this function returns an error status, the operation enters an error\0A * state and must be aborted by calling psa_pake_abort().\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation    Active PAKE operation.\0A * \5Cparam step                 The step for which the input is provided.\0A * \5Cparam[in] input            Buffer containing the input in the format\0A *                             appropriate for this \5Cp step. Refer to the\0A *                             documentation of the individual\0A *                             \5Cc PSA_PAKE_STEP_XXX constants for more\0A *                             information.\0A * \5Cparam input_length         Size of the \5Cp input buffer in bytes.\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS\0A *         Success.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_SIGNATURE\0A *         The verification fails for a #PSA_PAKE_STEP_ZK_PROOF input step.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\0A *         \5Cp input_length is not compatible with the \5Cp operation’s algorithm,\0A *         or the \5Cp input is not valid for the \5Cp operation's algorithm,\0A *         cipher suite or \5Cp step.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED\0A *         \5Cp step p is not supported with the \5Cp operation's algorithm, or the\0A *         \5Cp input is not supported for the \5Cp operation's algorithm, cipher\0A *         suite or \5Cp step.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_MEMORY \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_STORAGE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_DATA_CORRUPT \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_DATA_INVALID \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         The operation state is not valid (it must be active, and fully set\0A *         up, and this call must conform to the algorithm's requirements\0A *         for ordering of input and output steps), or\0A *         the library has not been previously initialized by psa_crypto_init().\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_pake_input(psa_pake_operation_t *operation,\0A                            psa_pake_step_t step,\0A                            const uint8_t *input,\0A                            size_t input_length);\0A\0A/** Get implicitly confirmed shared secret from a PAKE.\0A *\0A * At this point there is a cryptographic guarantee that only the authenticated\0A * party who used the same password is able to compute the key. But there is no\0A * guarantee that the peer is the party it claims to be and was able to do so.\0A *\0A * That is, the authentication is only implicit. Since the peer is not\0A * authenticated yet, no action should be taken yet that assumes that the peer\0A * is who it claims to be. For example, do not access restricted files on the\0A * peer's behalf until an explicit authentication has succeeded.\0A *\0A * This function can be called after the key exchange phase of the operation\0A * has completed. It imports the shared secret output of the PAKE into the\0A * provided derivation operation. The input step\0A * #PSA_KEY_DERIVATION_INPUT_SECRET is used when placing the shared key\0A * material in the key derivation operation.\0A *\0A * The exact sequence of calls to perform a password-authenticated key\0A * exchange depends on the algorithm in use.  Refer to the documentation of\0A * individual PAKE algorithm types (`PSA_ALG_XXX` values of type\0A * ::psa_algorithm_t such that #PSA_ALG_IS_PAKE(\5Cc alg) is true) for more\0A * information.\0A *\0A * When this function returns successfully, \5Cp operation becomes inactive.\0A * If this function returns an error status, both \5Cp operation\0A * and \5Cc key_derivation operations enter an error state and must be aborted by\0A * calling psa_pake_abort() and psa_key_derivation_abort() respectively.\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation    Active PAKE operation.\0A * \5Cparam[out] output          A key derivation operation that is ready\0A *                             for an input step of type\0A *                             #PSA_KEY_DERIVATION_INPUT_SECRET.\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS\0A *         Success.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\0A *         #PSA_KEY_DERIVATION_INPUT_SECRET is not compatible with the\0A *         algorithm in the \5Cp output key derivation operation.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED\0A *         Input from a PAKE is not supported by the algorithm in the \5Cp output\0A *         key derivation operation.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_MEMORY \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_STORAGE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_DATA_CORRUPT \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_DATA_INVALID \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         The PAKE operation state is not valid (it must be active, but beyond\0A *         that validity is specific to the algorithm), or\0A *         the library has not been previously initialized by psa_crypto_init(),\0A *         or the state of \5Cp output is not valid for\0A *         the #PSA_KEY_DERIVATION_INPUT_SECRET step. This can happen if the\0A *         step is out of order or the application has done this step already\0A *         and it may not be repeated.\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_pake_get_implicit_key(psa_pake_operation_t *operation,\0A                                       psa_key_derivation_operation_t *output);\0A\0A/** Abort a PAKE operation.\0A *\0A * Aborting an operation frees all associated resources except for the \5Cc\0A * operation structure itself. Once aborted, the operation object can be reused\0A * for another operation by calling psa_pake_setup() again.\0A *\0A * This function may be called at any time after the operation\0A * object has been initialized as described in #psa_pake_operation_t.\0A *\0A * In particular, calling psa_pake_abort() after the operation has been\0A * terminated by a call to psa_pake_abort() or psa_pake_get_implicit_key()\0A * is safe and has no effect.\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation    The operation to abort.\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS\0A *         Success.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         The library has not been previously initialized by psa_crypto_init().\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_pake_abort(psa_pake_operation_t *operation);\0A\0A/**@}*/\0A\0A/** A sufficient output buffer size for psa_pake_output().\0A *\0A * If the size of the output buffer is at least this large, it is guaranteed\0A * that psa_pake_output() will not fail due to an insufficient output buffer\0A * size. The actual size of the output might be smaller in any given call.\0A *\0A * See also #PSA_PAKE_OUTPUT_MAX_SIZE\0A *\0A * \5Cparam alg           A PAKE algorithm (\5Cc PSA_ALG_XXX value such that\0A *                      #PSA_ALG_IS_PAKE(\5Cp alg) is true).\0A * \5Cparam primitive     A primitive of type ::psa_pake_primitive_t that is\0A *                      compatible with algorithm \5Cp alg.\0A * \5Cparam output_step   A value of type ::psa_pake_step_t that is valid for the\0A *                      algorithm \5Cp alg.\0A * \5Creturn              A sufficient output buffer size for the specified\0A *                      PAKE algorithm, primitive, and output step. If the\0A *                      PAKE algorithm, primitive, or output step is not\0A *                      recognized, or the parameters are incompatible,\0A *                      return 0.\0A */\0A#define PSA_PAKE_OUTPUT_SIZE(alg, primitive, output_step)               \5C\0A    (alg == PSA_ALG_JPAKE &&                                           \5C\0A     primitive == PSA_PAKE_PRIMITIVE(PSA_PAKE_PRIMITIVE_TYPE_ECC,      \5C\0A                                     PSA_ECC_FAMILY_SECP_R1, 256) ?    \5C\0A     (                                                                 \5C\0A         output_step == PSA_PAKE_STEP_KEY_SHARE ? 65 :                   \5C\0A         output_step == PSA_PAKE_STEP_ZK_PUBLIC ? 65 :                   \5C\0A         32                                                              \5C\0A     ) :                                                               \5C\0A     0)\0A\0A/** A sufficient input buffer size for psa_pake_input().\0A *\0A * The value returned by this macro is guaranteed to be large enough for any\0A * valid input to psa_pake_input() in an operation with the specified\0A * parameters.\0A *\0A * See also #PSA_PAKE_INPUT_MAX_SIZE\0A *\0A * \5Cparam alg           A PAKE algorithm (\5Cc PSA_ALG_XXX value such that\0A *                      #PSA_ALG_IS_PAKE(\5Cp alg) is true).\0A * \5Cparam primitive     A primitive of type ::psa_pake_primitive_t that is\0A *                      compatible with algorithm \5Cp alg.\0A * \5Cparam input_step    A value of type ::psa_pake_step_t that is valid for the\0A *                      algorithm \5Cp alg.\0A * \5Creturn              A sufficient input buffer size for the specified\0A *                      input, cipher suite and algorithm. If the cipher suite,\0A *                      the input type or PAKE algorithm is not recognized, or\0A *                      the parameters are incompatible, return 0.\0A */\0A#define PSA_PAKE_INPUT_SIZE(alg, primitive, input_step)                 \5C\0A    (alg == PSA_ALG_JPAKE &&                                           \5C\0A     primitive == PSA_PAKE_PRIMITIVE(PSA_PAKE_PRIMITIVE_TYPE_ECC,      \5C\0A                                     PSA_ECC_FAMILY_SECP_R1, 256) ?    \5C\0A     (                                                                 \5C\0A         input_step == PSA_PAKE_STEP_KEY_SHARE ? 65 :                    \5C\0A         input_step == PSA_PAKE_STEP_ZK_PUBLIC ? 65 :                    \5C\0A         32                                                              \5C\0A     ) :                                                               \5C\0A     0)\0A\0A/** Output buffer size for psa_pake_output() for any of the supported PAKE\0A * algorithm and primitive suites and output step.\0A *\0A * This macro must expand to a compile-time constant integer.\0A *\0A * The value of this macro must be at least as large as the largest value\0A * returned by PSA_PAKE_OUTPUT_SIZE()\0A *\0A * See also #PSA_PAKE_OUTPUT_SIZE(\5Cp alg, \5Cp primitive, \5Cp output_step).\0A */\0A#define PSA_PAKE_OUTPUT_MAX_SIZE 65\0A\0A/** Input buffer size for psa_pake_input() for any of the supported PAKE\0A * algorithm and primitive suites and input step.\0A *\0A * This macro must expand to a compile-time constant integer.\0A *\0A * The value of this macro must be at least as large as the largest value\0A * returned by PSA_PAKE_INPUT_SIZE()\0A *\0A * See also #PSA_PAKE_INPUT_SIZE(\5Cp alg, \5Cp primitive, \5Cp output_step).\0A */\0A#define PSA_PAKE_INPUT_MAX_SIZE 65\0A\0A/** Returns a suitable initializer for a PAKE cipher suite object of type\0A * psa_pake_cipher_suite_t.\0A */\0A#define PSA_PAKE_CIPHER_SUITE_INIT { PSA_ALG_NONE, 0, 0, 0, PSA_ALG_NONE }\0A\0A/** Returns a suitable initializer for a PAKE operation object of type\0A * psa_pake_operation_t.\0A */\0A#if defined(MBEDTLS_PSA_CRYPTO_CLIENT) && !defined(MBEDTLS_PSA_CRYPTO_C)\0A#define PSA_PAKE_OPERATION_INIT { 0 }\0A#else\0A#define PSA_PAKE_OPERATION_INIT { 0, PSA_ALG_NONE, 0, PSA_PAKE_OPERATION_STAGE_SETUP, \5C\0A                                  { 0 }, { { 0 } } }\0A#endif\0A\0Astruct psa_pake_cipher_suite_s {\0A    psa_algorithm_t algorithm;\0A    psa_pake_primitive_type_t type;\0A    psa_pake_family_t family;\0A    uint16_t  bits;\0A    psa_algorithm_t hash;\0A};\0A\0Astatic inline psa_algorithm_t psa_pake_cs_get_algorithm(\0A    const psa_pake_cipher_suite_t *cipher_suite)\0A{\0A    return cipher_suite->algorithm;\0A}\0A\0Astatic inline void psa_pake_cs_set_algorithm(\0A    psa_pake_cipher_suite_t *cipher_suite,\0A    psa_algorithm_t algorithm)\0A{\0A    if (!PSA_ALG_IS_PAKE(algorithm)) {\0A        cipher_suite->algorithm = 0;\0A    } else {\0A        cipher_suite->algorithm = algorithm;\0A    }\0A}\0A\0Astatic inline psa_pake_primitive_t psa_pake_cs_get_primitive(\0A    const psa_pake_cipher_suite_t *cipher_suite)\0A{\0A    return PSA_PAKE_PRIMITIVE(cipher_suite->type, cipher_suite->family,\0A                              cipher_suite->bits);\0A}\0A\0Astatic inline void psa_pake_cs_set_primitive(\0A    psa_pake_cipher_suite_t *cipher_suite,\0A    psa_pake_primitive_t primitive)\0A{\0A    cipher_suite->type = (psa_pake_primitive_type_t) (primitive >> 24);\0A    cipher_suite->family = (psa_pake_family_t) (0xFF & (primitive >> 16));\0A    cipher_suite->bits = (uint16_t) (0xFFFF & primitive);\0A}\0A\0Astatic inline psa_pake_family_t psa_pake_cs_get_family(\0A    const psa_pake_cipher_suite_t *cipher_suite)\0A{\0A    return cipher_suite->family;\0A}\0A\0Astatic inline uint16_t psa_pake_cs_get_bits(\0A    const psa_pake_cipher_suite_t *cipher_suite)\0A{\0A    return cipher_suite->bits;\0A}\0A\0Astatic inline psa_algorithm_t psa_pake_cs_get_hash(\0A    const psa_pake_cipher_suite_t *cipher_suite)\0A{\0A    return cipher_suite->hash;\0A}\0A\0Astatic inline void psa_pake_cs_set_hash(psa_pake_cipher_suite_t *cipher_suite,\0A                                        psa_algorithm_t hash)\0A{\0A    if (!PSA_ALG_IS_HASH(hash)) {\0A        cipher_suite->hash = 0;\0A    } else {\0A        cipher_suite->hash = hash;\0A    }\0A}\0A\0Astruct psa_crypto_driver_pake_inputs_s {\0A    uint8_t *MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(password);\0A    size_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(password_len);\0A    uint8_t *MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(user);\0A    size_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(user_len);\0A    uint8_t *MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(peer);\0A    size_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(peer_len);\0A    psa_key_attributes_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(attributes);\0A    psa_pake_cipher_suite_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(cipher_suite);\0A};\0A\0Atypedef enum psa_crypto_driver_pake_step {\0A    PSA_JPAKE_STEP_INVALID        = 0,  /* Invalid step */\0A    PSA_JPAKE_X1_STEP_KEY_SHARE   = 1,  /* Round 1: input/output key share (for ephemeral private key X1).*/\0A    PSA_JPAKE_X1_STEP_ZK_PUBLIC   = 2,  /* Round 1: input/output Schnorr NIZKP public key for the X1 key */\0A    PSA_JPAKE_X1_STEP_ZK_PROOF    = 3,  /* Round 1: input/output Schnorr NIZKP proof for the X1 key */\0A    PSA_JPAKE_X2_STEP_KEY_SHARE   = 4,  /* Round 1: input/output key share (for ephemeral private key X2).*/\0A    PSA_JPAKE_X2_STEP_ZK_PUBLIC   = 5,  /* Round 1: input/output Schnorr NIZKP public key for the X2 key */\0A    PSA_JPAKE_X2_STEP_ZK_PROOF    = 6,  /* Round 1: input/output Schnorr NIZKP proof for the X2 key */\0A    PSA_JPAKE_X2S_STEP_KEY_SHARE  = 7,  /* Round 2: output X2S key (our key) */\0A    PSA_JPAKE_X2S_STEP_ZK_PUBLIC  = 8,  /* Round 2: output Schnorr NIZKP public key for the X2S key (our key) */\0A    PSA_JPAKE_X2S_STEP_ZK_PROOF   = 9,  /* Round 2: output Schnorr NIZKP proof for the X2S key (our key) */\0A    PSA_JPAKE_X4S_STEP_KEY_SHARE  = 10, /* Round 2: input X4S key (from peer) */\0A    PSA_JPAKE_X4S_STEP_ZK_PUBLIC  = 11, /* Round 2: input Schnorr NIZKP public key for the X4S key (from peer) */\0A    PSA_JPAKE_X4S_STEP_ZK_PROOF   = 12  /* Round 2: input Schnorr NIZKP proof for the X4S key (from peer) */\0A} psa_crypto_driver_pake_step_t;\0A\0Atypedef enum psa_jpake_round {\0A    PSA_JPAKE_FIRST = 0,\0A    PSA_JPAKE_SECOND = 1,\0A    PSA_JPAKE_FINISHED = 2\0A} psa_jpake_round_t;\0A\0Atypedef enum psa_jpake_io_mode {\0A    PSA_JPAKE_INPUT = 0,\0A    PSA_JPAKE_OUTPUT = 1\0A} psa_jpake_io_mode_t;\0A\0Astruct psa_jpake_computation_stage_s {\0A    /* The J-PAKE round we are currently on */\0A    psa_jpake_round_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(round);\0A    /* The 'mode' we are currently in (inputting or outputting) */\0A    psa_jpake_io_mode_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(io_mode);\0A    /* The number of completed inputs so far this round */\0A    uint8_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(inputs);\0A    /* The number of completed outputs so far this round */\0A    uint8_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(outputs);\0A    /* The next expected step (KEY_SHARE, ZK_PUBLIC or ZK_PROOF) */\0A    psa_pake_step_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(step);\0A};\0A\0A#define PSA_JPAKE_EXPECTED_INPUTS(round) ((round) == PSA_JPAKE_FINISHED ? 0 : \5C\0A                                          ((round) == PSA_JPAKE_FIRST ? 2 : 1))\0A#define PSA_JPAKE_EXPECTED_OUTPUTS(round) ((round) == PSA_JPAKE_FINISHED ? 0 : \5C\0A                                           ((round) == PSA_JPAKE_FIRST ? 2 : 1))\0A\0Astruct psa_pake_operation_s {\0A#if defined(MBEDTLS_PSA_CRYPTO_CLIENT) && !defined(MBEDTLS_PSA_CRYPTO_C)\0A    mbedtls_psa_client_handle_t handle;\0A#else\0A    /** Unique ID indicating which driver got assigned to do the\0A     * operation. Since driver contexts are driver-specific, swapping\0A     * drivers halfway through the operation is not supported.\0A     * ID values are auto-generated in psa_crypto_driver_wrappers.h\0A     * ID value zero means the context is not valid or not assigned to\0A     * any driver (i.e. none of the driver contexts are active). */\0A    unsigned int MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(id);\0A    /* Algorithm of the PAKE operation */\0A    psa_algorithm_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(alg);\0A    /* A primitive of type compatible with algorithm */\0A    psa_pake_primitive_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(primitive);\0A    /* Stage of the PAKE operation: waiting for the setup, collecting inputs\0A     * or computing. */\0A    uint8_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(stage);\0A    /* Holds computation stage of the PAKE algorithms. */\0A    union {\0A        uint8_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(dummy);\0A#if defined(PSA_WANT_ALG_JPAKE)\0A        psa_jpake_computation_stage_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(jpake);\0A#endif\0A    } MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(computation_stage);\0A    union {\0A        psa_driver_pake_context_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(ctx);\0A        psa_crypto_driver_pake_inputs_t MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(inputs);\0A    } MBEDTLS_PRIVATE(data);\0A#endif\0A};\0A\0Astatic inline struct psa_pake_cipher_suite_s psa_pake_cipher_suite_init(void)\0A{\0A    const struct psa_pake_cipher_suite_s v = PSA_PAKE_CIPHER_SUITE_INIT;\0A    return v;\0A}\0A\0Astatic inline struct psa_pake_operation_s psa_pake_operation_init(void)\0A{\0A    const struct psa_pake_operation_s v = PSA_PAKE_OPERATION_INIT;\0A    return v;\0A}\0A\0A#ifdef __cplusplus\0A}\0A#endif\0A\0A#endif /* PSA_CRYPTO_EXTRA_H */\0A\00" }
