t[Unit, String] =\0A    if os_remove_tree_raw(path) == 0 { Ok(()) }\0A    else { Err(\22Os.remove_tree: could not remove \22.concat(path).concat(\22: \22).concat(unsafe { plum_tree_last_error().as_string() })) }\0A\0A/// Copies the contents of `src` into the existing directory `dst`.\0A/// Both roots must be ordinary directories, even with trailing separators;\0A/// their ancestors resolve normally. Identical or nested roots return `Err`\0A/// before changing `dst`. Links inside `src` are copied as links, including\0A/// dangling links, without reading their targets. Destination links and\0A/// unsupported Windows reparse points are rejected. Failure to recreate a\0A/// link returns `Err` rather than substituting its target or link text.\0A/// Regular destination files are replaced, so other hardlinks are unchanged.\0A/// Traversal uses held directories, at most 128 levels, and a 64 KiB transfer\0A/// buffer independent of file size. Errors can leave partial output; the\0A/// caller owns cleanup. File modes are not preserved.\0A/// Errors include both requested roots and the recorded refusal or native failure.\0Apub let copy_tree (src: String) (dst: String): Result[Unit, String] =\0A    if os_copy_tree_raw(src, dst) == 0 { Ok(()) }\0A    else { Err(\22Os.copy_tree: could not copy \22.concat(src).concat(\22 to \22).concat(dst).concat(\22: \22).concat(unsafe { plum_tree_last_error().as_string() })) }\0A\0A// --- Environment and process ---\0A//\0A// Folded in from the flat prelude in 0.0.9. `Os` already owned the\0A// filesystem calls that shell out to `os_shim.c`, so putting\0A// `read_file` in a separate `Fs` would have split the filesystem\0A// across two modules. This is the shape Go settled on -- `os.ReadFile`,\0A// `os.Getenv`, `os.Exit`, `os.MkdirAll` in one place, with `net`\0A// separate and string helpers on the type.\0A\0Alet exit_raw (code: Int): Bool = false\0Alet env_var_raw (name: String): Array[Bytes] = []\0A\0A/// Exit with a status code, printing not